{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 5472895757856360673, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 636, "mtime": 1791865380.5642889, "sha256": "178db903bdff09e3efcb70538852806a06ab1345cb91e4b0b945b44860d44772"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 418, "mtime": 1791865383.5445526, "sha256": "96a4155b08143e8348bc5cde79167f7ed5bae089cf632056192b8dd937d97189"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/5/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/5/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test that covers the reported case, the round-half-to-even trap, and negative values:\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** `2.675` can't be stored exactly as a float. Its real value is `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. `round` also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit (`0.125` \u2192 `0.12`), which doesn't match the \"half up\" the docstring promises.\n\n**Fix** in `pricing/money.py`: convert the price with `Decimal(str(x))`. `str` gives the number as people read it (`\"2.675\"`), and `quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), ROUND_HALF_UP)` then rounds it half up. The function still returns a `float`, so callers don't change.\n\n**Check:** I compared the new function with the built-in `round` (2 decimals) on a few inputs:\n\n| input | `round_money` | `round(x, 2)` |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2.675 | 2.68 | 2.67 |\n| 0.125 | 0.13 | 0.12 |\n| 1.005 | 1.01 | 1.0 |\n| 2.674 | 2.67 | 2.67 |\n| -2.675 | -2.68 | -2.67 |\n\n`add_vat(10)` still gives `12.0` and `split(10.00, 3)` still gives `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`.\n\nI added `tests/test_round_money.py` with these cases, but haven't run it or the existing tests: pytest isn't installed here. The results above come from calling the functions directly.\n\n**Remaining risk:** `add_vat` multiplies floats before rounding (`x * (1 + rate)`). If that product lands just under a half-cent (e.g. `\u20264999999998`), `str` shows that exact value and it still rounds down. Fully avoiding this means doing the VAT arithmetic in `Decimal` as well. I didn't change that because it's outside what you asked for.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 251134, "requests_cache_write": 10582, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1503968, "requests_count": 9, "request